<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12 text-[var(--foreground)] leading-relaxed">
  
  <!-- Main Section Header -->
  <div class="text-center space-y-3">
    <span class="text-xs uppercase font-bold tracking-widest text-cyan-400 px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/20">
      Comprehensive On-Page SEO Guide & Documentation
    </span>
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
      The Complete Favicon Size & Online Favicon Generator Guide
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      Discover what is a favicon, standard favicon size specifications for modern web platforms, supported favicon formats, and how our free favicon maker converts PNG to favicon packages in seconds.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Article 1: What is a Favicon? Meaning & History -->
  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-lg space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)] flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-indigo-500/15 text-indigo-400 font-mono text-sm flex items-center justify-center font-black">
        01
      </span>
      What is a Favicon? Understanding Favicon Meaning and Importance
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
      Have you ever wondered <strong>what is a favicon</strong> and why almost every website on the internet displays a small graphic in your browser tab? The word <em>favicon</em> is a portmanteau of the words "favorite" and "icon." In web design terminology, the <strong>favicon meaning</strong> refers to the tiny visual icon associated with a particular website, web page, or web application. When visitors bookmark your URL, browse multiple open tabs, or discover your link on mobile search engine results pages, the <strong>favicon</strong> serves as the primary visual anchor representing your brand identity.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
      Originally introduced in 1999 with Microsoft Internet Explorer 5, the earliest <strong>favicon format</strong> was strictly a 16×16 pixel graphic stored as a Windows ICO file in the root directory of a web server. Today, <strong>what is favicon</strong> has evolved into a sophisticated multi-device identity system. Modern browsers, mobile operating systems like Apple iOS and Google Android, search engines, and Progressive Web Apps (PWAs) all query your website for custom dimensions. If a site lacks a properly formatted icon, browsers display a generic empty document icon, signaling an unpolished or insecure digital presence to users.
    </p>
  </article>

  <!-- Article 2: What Size Should a Favicon Be? -->
  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-lg space-y-5">
    <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)] flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/15 text-cyan-400 font-mono text-sm flex items-center justify-center font-black">
        02
      </span>
      What Size Should a Favicon Be? The Standard Favicon Size Guide
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
      A frequent question among frontend developers and webmasters is: <strong>what size should a favicon be</strong>, and what is the <strong>standard favicon size</strong> for website deployment? Because devices range from compact smartphones to ultra-high-density 5K Retina computer displays, there is no longer just one single dimension. Instead, a modern <strong>favicon size</strong> strategy relies on standard resolutions engineered for specific display contexts.
    </p>

    <!-- Detailed Size Table -->
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)]">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
        <thead class="bg-[var(--muted)]/50 border-b border-[var(--border)] text-[var(--muted-foreground)] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
          <tr>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Standard Favicon Size</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Target Environment</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Recommended Format</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Role & Importance</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-[var(--border)]">
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">16×16 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Classic Desktop Browser Tab</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">ICO / PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">The classic standard favicon size for 1x displays, address bars, and history lists.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">32×32 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Retina & 4K Browser Tabs</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG / ICO</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">Essential high-DPI desktop tab icon; default desktop resolution for crisp rendering.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">48×48 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Google SERP Search Result</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">Strictly required by Googlebot search crawler (must be multiple of 48px square).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">96×96 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Google TV & Desktop Shortcut</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">High-resolution desktop bookmarks, shortcut tiles, and smart TV app trays.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">180×180 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Apple Touch Icon (iOS)</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">Required for iPhone and iPad home screen shortcuts; iOS applies squircle mask.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">192×192 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">Android Chrome PWA Launch</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">Progressive Web App launch icon declared in site.webmanifest for Android.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="hover:bg-[var(--accent)]/30">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400">512×512 px</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--foreground)]">PWA Splash Screen & Store</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono">PNG</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">High-resolution loading splash screen and Google Play store presentation icon.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">
      When planning your <strong>favicon size for website</strong> production, starting with a square 512×512 px master graphic ensures all downscaled assets remain crystal clear.
    </p>
  </article>

  <!-- Article 3: Choosing the Right Favicon Format -->
  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-lg space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)] flex items-center gap-3">
      <span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/15 text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm flex items-center justify-center font-black">
        03
      </span>
      Selecting the Best Favicon Format: ICO, PNG, or Modern SVG?
    </h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
      Choosing the correct <strong>favicon format</strong> is just as essential as maintaining the right dimensions. Over the years, the web development ecosystem has embraced three primary formats:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--muted)]/20 space-y-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-purple-400">1. Scalable Vector (SVG)</span>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          The undisputed modern champion. An SVG favicon scales infinitely from 16 pixels up to billboard sizes with zero loss of quality, all while keeping file sizes microscopic (often under 2 KB). Even better, SVG supports embedded CSS media queries, enabling your icon to dynamically toggle colors when a user switches between light mode and dark mode via <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">prefers-color-scheme</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--muted)]/20 space-y-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-emerald-400">2. Raster Alpha (PNG)</span>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          The most versatile raster format. PNG delivers 32-bit RGBA color with full alpha transparency, making it the industry standard for Apple Touch Icons (180×180) and Android PWA manifests (192×192 and 512×512).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--muted)]/20 space-y-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-cyan-400">3. Classic Container (ICO)</span>
        <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          While older, the ICO container remains irreplaceable as a universal fallback. A properly packaged ICO file can hold multiple bitmap resolutions (both 16×16 and 32×32) inside a single binary structure. It ensures complete backward compatibility with older browsers, legacy RSS aggregators, and search engine bots that probe directly for <code class="font-mono text-[11px]">/favicon.ico</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Article 4: Why You Need a Favicon Generator & Maker -->
  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-lg space-y-4">
