    <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-800 bg-[#0f141c] p-4 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-200 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed">
      <pre><code>&lt;!-- Modern Favicon Suite by Favvicon.com --&gt;
&lt;link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"&gt;
&lt;link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32"&gt;
&lt;link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png"&gt;
&lt;link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"&gt;
&lt;meta name="theme-color" content="#13141f"&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>

    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed">
      Whether you are building a personal portfolio, an enterprise SaaS application, or an e-commerce storefront, knowing <strong>what is a favicon?</strong> and adhering to <strong>standard favicon size</strong> specifications is fundamental to modern web design. Use our instant <strong>favicon generator</strong> to convert <strong>png to favicon</strong> assets, validate your dimensions across every device, and ensure your website makes an unforgettable impression.
    </p>
  </article>

</section>
